 <main id="main"><article>
 <header><h1>An exact period criterion for focal-distance products in elliptic billiards</h1><p>Alec Kriebel · 11 October 2026 · Native deposit version 1.0.0 · Unrefereed preprint</p><p><a href="https://orcid.org/0009-0001-9320-500X">ORCID</a> · <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23306203">DOI and Zenodo record</a></p></header>
 <section id="abstract"><h2>Original printed abstract</h2><p>For a noncircular elliptic billiard with a strictly nested nondegenerate confocal elliptical caustic, we prove that the product of ordinary distances from all vertices to either fixed focus is independent of phase if and only if the least period is 2 modulo 4. This proves the least-period interpretation of entry k₁₁₄ in Reznik–Garcia–Koiller&#x27;s list of unproved invariants and classifies every other primitive period and every repeated traversal. The proof identifies the complete divisor of the focal-distance factor in the classical Jacobi parameter. An exact doubled-triangle example shows why a condition on return length alone is insufficient. The parametrization, identities and divisor method are established tools. This AI-assisted research note is unrefereed.</p></section>
