 <section id="references"><h2>Related literature</h2><ul><li><a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/s40598-021-00174-y">Reznik–Garcia–Koiller: Fifty New Invariants of N-Periodics in the Elliptic Billiard</a>. Final 2021 article, definitions and Table 2 k₁₁₄; observed invariant credit.</li><li><a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/s40879-021-00524-2">Stachel: On the motion of billiards in ellipses</a>. Published 2022 Theorem 4.3 and equation (4.9): canonical parametrization.</li><li><a href="https://dlmf.nist.gov/22">NIST DLMF, Chapter 22</a>. Classical Jacobi periods, poles, shifts and addition formulas.</li><li><a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.geomphys.2014.07.024">Schwartz: The pentagram integrals for Poncelet families</a>. Established meromorphic Poncelet and pole-removal method.</li><li><a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/s40879-020-00426-9">Akopyan–Schwartz–Tabachnikov: Billiards in ellipses revisited</a>. Classical complexification and pole-cancellation context.</li><li><a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/s40598-021-00188-6">Roitman–Garcia–Reznik: New Invariants of Poncelet–Jacobi Bicentric Polygons</a>. Related Jacobi/Liouville methods, with different invariants.</li><li><a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23093258">Ferudun: Focal Distance Products of Outer Elliptic Billiard Polygons</a>. Related unrefereed k₁₁₅ note; distinct outer-tangent vertices and byte-custody limit.</li><li><a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.physd.2023.133776">Dragović–Gajić: Points with rotational ellipsoids of inertia, envelopes of hyperplanes which equally fit the system of points in ℝᵏ, and ellipsoidal billiards</a>. Related article whose full billiard body remains a disclosed coverage gap.</li></ul></section>
